DepositCoreX - Core Banking Deposits, Interest & 
GL Posting Management System
1. Introduction
DepositCoreX is a web-based Core Banking Deposits & Account Servicing System
designed for banks to manage Savings, Current, and Term Deposit (FD/RD) products.
It handles end-to-end lifecycle activities:
• CASA & Term deposit account creation
• Standing instructions
• Interest accrual & posting
• Cheque book & debit card references
• Transaction ledgering & GL posting
• Dormancy, holds, lien marking
• Account closure, payouts
• Regulatory & operational reports
The platform uses a REST API-based backend architecture with Angular/React frontend, 
compatible with Java (Spring Boot) or .NET (ASP.NET Core).
Actors / Users
• Customer: Views balances, deposits, statements.
• Branch Officer: Opens accounts, manages customer servicing requests.
• Operations Officer: Handles transitions, holds, FD/RD servicing.
• Finance/GL Analyst: Oversees GL posting and settlements.
• Core Admin: Configures deposit products, interest tables, charges, rules.
2. Module Overview
2.1 Identity & Access Management
Authentication, RBAC, audit logs.
2.2 Customer Onboarding Reference
Customer KYC profile linking (read-only reference from KYC system).
2.3 CASA & Term Deposit Account Creation
Account number generation, linkage, product details.
2.4 Deposit Product Configuration
CASA, FD, RD parameters — interest tables, TDS rules, charges.
2.5 Transaction Ledgering & GL Posting
Debit/credit postings, reversal, fees, and GL entries.
2.6 Interest Accrual & Posting
Daily accrual for CASA; maturity schedule for FD/RD.
2.7 Standing Instructions, Holds & Lien Marking
Account holds, SI executions, lien freeze, partial freeze.
2.8 Account Servicing (FD/RD lifecycle)
Premature closure, renewal, maturity payouts.
2.9 Statements, SOA & Regulatory Reporting
Monthly statements, interest certificates, regulatory reports.
2.10 Notifications & Alerts
Balace alerts, FD maturity, charges, SI failures.
3. Architecture Overview
• Frontend: Angular/React
• Backend: REST microservices
• Database: MySQL/PostgreSQL/SQL Server
• Integration: No external CBS/GL integration in Phase-1 (placeholder only)
