7. User Interface Design
• Customer Portal: Balance, statements, interest credit history, FD/RD summary.
• Branch Dashboard: Account opening, servicing requests, SI setup, holds.
• Operations Console: Disbursement, renewal, maturity payouts, premature closures.
• Finance Dashboard: GL posting view, ledger trial balances, reconciliation.
• Admin Panel: Products, interest tables, charges, user roles, reports.
8. Non-Functional Requirements
• Performance: 50,000 concurrent users and high-volume accounts/transactions.
• Security: PII encryption, RBAC, audit trails, compliance-ready.
• Scalability: Multi-branch, multi-product core banking support.
• Availability: 99.9% uptime.
• Maintainability: Modular services, API versioning, batch jobs for daily processes.
• Observability: Core banking KPIs, logs, GL mismatch alerts.
9. Assumptions & Constraints
• No real-time integration to external CBS or SWIFT in Phase-1 (internal ledger only).
• Interest calculation uses internal job scheduler (no third-party engine).
• Notifications are in-app only.
• Fully implementable using Java Spring Boot/ASP.NET Core, Angular/React + 
RDBMS
